The fix is in src/renderer/src/editor/captionItems.ts only. Replace the shared `cancelled` flag with a per-call generation counter, and treat a "Cancelled." rejection as a cancel, not a failure. The AiError kind does not survive the IPC call, so the renderer has to match on the message text.

```ts
let generation = 0
const isCancel = (msg: string): boolean => /^(AiError: )?Cancelled\.$/.test(msg)

export async function transcribe({ store }, options) {
  const projectId = store.state.id
  if (job?.running) return false
  const mine = ++generation
  setJob({ projectId, progress: null, error: null, running: true })
  const off = window.api.onTranscribeProgress((progress) => { if (mine === generation && progress.projectId === projectId && job?.running) setJob({ ...job, progress }) })
  try {
    const raw = await window.api.transcribe(projectId, options)
    if (mine !== generation) return false
    ...unchanged...
  } catch (err) {
    if (mine !== generation) return false
    const message = ipcMessage(err)
    setJob(isCancel(message) ? null : { projectId, progress: null, error: message, running: false })
    return false
  } finally { off() }
}

export function cancelTranscription(): void {
  if (!job?.running) return
  generation++                       // drop the late result or error of the cancelled call
  const id = job.projectId
  setJob({ ...job, progress: null }) // still running, so Generate stays hidden until main has stopped
  void window.api.cancelTranscription(id).catch(() => undefined).finally(() => { if (job?.projectId === id && job.running) setJob(null) })
}
```

- isCancel() fixes (a): closing the editor no longer leaves an error behind.
- The generation check plus keeping the job running until cancelTranscription resolves fixes (b): main no longer refuses the second start with "already being transcribed", and a stale rejection cannot overwrite a newer job.
- Optional: show "Stopping…" in CaptionsPanel while the job is in that state.

Fix it in the main process, where the window is hidden, so it covers every way `prepare` can fail. In `src/main/recordingIpc.ts`, change the `recording:prepare` handler to show the main window again when preparing fails and no recording is active:

```ts
ipcMain.handle('recording:prepare', (_e, request: RecordingRequest) =>
  prepare(request).catch((err: unknown) => {
    // A restarted take keeps the main window hidden (endRecordingUi(true)); if the next take cannot
    // even be prepared, bring the app back so the error is seen.
    const main = getMainWindow()
    if (!active && main && !main.isDestroyed() && !main.isVisible()) {
      main.show()
      main.focus()
    }
    throw err
  })
)
```

- When a first take fails to prepare, the window is already visible, so nothing changes.
- The `!active` guard leaves the "A recording is already in progress" refusal alone.
- No renderer or API change is needed.

Optionally, a `restartPending` flag set in `endRecordingUi(true)` and cleared on a successful `prepare` would narrow the condition. It is not required.

Fix it in the main process only, in src/main/recordingIpc.ts, so that every caller is covered. Wrap the prepare handler so that a failed prepare brings the hidden main window back when no recording is active:

  ipcMain.handle('recording:prepare', async (_e, request: RecordingRequest) => {
    try {
      return await prepare(request)
    } catch (err) {
      // After a Restart the main window is still hidden: show it, so the error can be seen.
      const main = getMainWindow()
      if (!active && main && !main.isDestroyed() && !main.isVisible()) { main.show(); main.focus() }
      throw err
    }
  })

The `!active` guard leaves the window hidden when the failure is "A recording is already in progress". The `!isVisible()` guard makes this a no-op when a first take fails from Home, where the window is already showing. No renderer change is needed. Home's existing catch already shows the error once the window is visible.

Optional extra: also reset the toolbar state. hideToolbar already ran in endRecordingUi(true), so nothing more is needed for that.
